msgstr "Solution 1: The Ascend compiler has a corresponding solution for the coreDim exceeding limit issue. Simply set the environment variable 'TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL' to 1. The setting command is as follows:"

msgid "解决思路2： 通过增大 BLOCK_SIZE 来减少所需的核心数量，确保 coreDim 不超过限制。 计算公式如下："
msgstr "Solution 2: Increase the BLOCK_SIZE to reduce the number of required cores, ensuring that coreDim does not exceed the limit. The calculation formula is as follows:"

msgid "代入 `N = 1073741824` 可得："
msgstr "Substituting `N = 1073741824` yields:"

msgid "因此，如果 `BLOCK_SIZE` 按 2 的幂取值，至少应设置为 `32768`。"
msgstr "Therefore, if `BLOCK_SIZE` takes a power of 2, it should be set to at least `32768`."

msgid "优化前的代码："
msgstr "Code before optimization:"

msgid "优化后的代码："
msgstr "Optimized code:"

msgid "动态计算适合的 BLOCK_SIZE 以避免 coreDim 超限"
msgstr "Dynamically calculate the appropriate BLOCK_SIZE to avoid exceeding the coreDim limit."

msgid "处理复合问题：coreDim + UB 溢出"
msgstr "Handling composite issues: coreDim + UB overflow"

msgid "问题分析: 在某些情况下，解决了 coreDim 问题后可能引发新的UB溢出问题。这通常发生在增大 BLOCK_SIZE 后，单个线程块需要处理的数据量超出了NPU的UB缓存容量。"
msgstr "Problem Analysis: In some cases, resolving the coreDim issue may introduce new UB overflow problems. This typically occurs when, after increasing BLOCK_SIZE, the amount of data that a single thread block needs to process exceeds the UB cache capacity of the NPU."

msgid "案例： 数据规模：N = 1073741824，原始 BLOCK_SIZE = 4096，计算得到的 coreDim = 262144 > 65535（超限），调整为 BLOCK_SIZE = 32768 后，coreDim = 32768（合规），但出现 UB 溢出"
msgstr "Case: Data size: N = 1073741824, original BLOCK_SIZE = 4096, calculated coreDim = 262144 > 65535 (exceeds limit). After adjusting BLOCK_SIZE = 32768, coreDim = 32768 (compliant), but UB overflow occurs."

msgid "解决思路： 引入 BLOCK_SIZE_SUB 参数，将大块进一步细分，在保持合理 coreDim 的同时控制内存使用。 优化前代码："
msgstr "Solution: Introduce the BLOCK_SIZE_SUB parameter to further subdivide large blocks, controlling memory usage while maintaining a reasonable coreDim. Code before optimization:"

msgid "优化后代码："
msgstr "Optimized code:"

msgid "为什么会出现UBSIZE超出内存的错误"
msgstr "Why does the UBSIZE out-of-memory error occur?"

msgid "切分不合理,存在过多的非对齐访存或者运算，例如对（64，32）二维数据搬运，对应stride(12832，128),如果是对齐数据的访存，对应的stride(32,1)。 对于非对齐访问内容，在最内轴新增一个大小为1的轴，变为（64，32，4） 由于硬件要求vector算子场景ub内存32bytes对齐 ，假设type=float16，对应stride应该为(12832, 128,1)"
msgstr "Unreasonable segmentation leads to excessive non-aligned memory access or computation. For example, when moving two-dimensional data of (64, 32), the corresponding stride is (12832, 128). If it is aligned memory access, the corresponding stride is (32, 1). For non-aligned access content, add a new axis of size 1 to the innermost axis, changing it to (64, 32, 4). Since the hardware requires 32-byte alignment of UB memory in vector operator scenarios, assuming type=float16, the corresponding stride should be (12832, 128, 1)."

msgid "离散访存代码逐行对比观察scalar低效映射"
msgstr "Line-by-line comparison of discrete memory access code to observe scalar inefficient mapping"

msgid "设置环境变量TRITON_DEBUG=1, 保存~/.triton/cache/xxx.ttadapter，然后执行"
msgstr "Set the environment variable TRITON_DEBUG=1, save ~/.triton/cache/xxx.ttadapter, and then execute"

msgid "会有输出IR ， 对比Triton 算子逻辑与IR内部的操作，观察是否有未映射成指令的操作。 观察HIVM IR阶段是否存在纯scalar搬运或者计算， 没有映射为simd指令，这会成为性能瓶颈。"
msgstr "There will be an output IR. Compare the Triton operator logic with the operations inside the IR to observe whether there are any unmapped operations. Check whether there are pure scalar transfers or computations in the HIVM IR stage that are not mapped to SIMD instructions, as this could become a performance bottleneck."

msgid "问题：离散访存 && scalar低效映射 b[1024, 32] = a[1024, 32]  Triton原先写法利用thread的方式 对[1024,32] 中的最低维度32绑定线程块, 再对1024切16，分为[64， 16， 32]，再对64绑定线程块"
msgstr "Problem: Discontinuous memory access && scalar inefficient mapping b[1024, 32] = a[1024, 32]. The original Triton implementation uses threads to bind the lowest dimension 32 in [1024, 32] to thread blocks, then splits 1024 into 16, resulting in [64, 16, 32], and finally binds 64 to thread blocks."

msgid "优化思路"
msgstr "Optimization Approach"

msgid "调整 block_ptr 的 shape/stride: 把 (1024, 32) 看成二维矩阵，最低维度 32 是连续的，所以 stride 应该是 (32, 1)，而不是 (32,)，这样每个线程块能访问连续的 32 元素。让线程块绑定到行维度（1024），每个线程处理一整行的 32 元素。这样访存就是连续的，亲和性好。"
msgstr "Adjust the shape/stride of `block_ptr`: treat (1024, 32) as a two-dimensional matrix, where the lowest dimension 32 is contiguous, so the stride should be (32, 1) instead of (32,), allowing each thread block to access contiguous 32 elements. Bind the thread block to the row dimension (1024), with each thread processing an entire row of 32 elements. This ensures contiguous memory access and good locality."

msgid "比如："
msgstr "For example:"

msgid "NPU高性能编程指南"
msgstr "NPU High-Performance Programming Guide"

msgid "合并Grid分核"
msgstr "Merge Grid Core Splitting"

msgid "一、自动合并Grid分核优化原则"
msgstr "I. Principles for Automatic Merging of Grid Core Division Optimization"

msgid "部分场景下，Triton算子从GPU迁移到NPU。由于体系结构的差异，基于GPU开发的Triton算子Grid分核数较多。在NPU上执行时，无法一次全部调度，多轮下发导致下发时延过大，影响算子性能。基于NPU优Triton算子过程中，需要首先检查Grid分核数。当分核数较大时，使用TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL环境变量提升算子执行性能。"
msgstr "In some scenarios, Triton operators are migrated from GPU to NPU. Due to architectural differences, Triton operators developed on GPU have a large number of grid blocks. When executed on NPU, they cannot be fully scheduled at once, and multiple rounds of dispatch lead to excessive dispatch latency, affecting operator performance. During the optimization of Triton operators on NPU, it is necessary to first check the number of grid blocks. When the number of blocks is large, use the `TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL` environment variable to improve operator execution performance."

msgid "指令并行优化"
msgstr "Instruction Parallel Optimization"

msgid "一、指令并行优化核心原则"
msgstr "I. Core Principles of Instruction Parallelism Optimization"

msgid "Triton算子在NPU上执行时，为了提升性能，NPU底层提供multi buffer、指令并行等并行机制，将“数据搬入/数据计算/数据搬出”并行起来，以此来提升性能；但是某些场景下存在multi buffer无法使能问题，影响并行度，导致算子执行性能降低；在性能优化过程中，存在此类问题时，可以参考以下几点做排查，并按照代码示例优化： 1、数据搬运和计算存在数据依赖，产生同步，必须依赖Vector运算后，才能触发MTE搬运，导致并行度低； 2、算子内，无多个数据加载或者单次执行完成无Tiling切分，该场景下无法使能multi buffer； 3、multi buffer需要额外增加UB空间的使用，计算过程中UB空间不足，无法使能multi buffer；"
msgstr "When Triton operators execute on the NPU, to improve performance, the NPU底层 provides parallel mechanisms such as multi-buffer and instruction parallelism to parallelize \"data loading / data computation / data unloading,\" thereby enhancing performance. However, in certain scenarios, multi-buffer may fail to be enabled, affecting parallelism and leading to reduced operator execution performance. During performance optimization, if such issues arise, you can refer to the following points for troubleshooting and optimize according to the code examples: 1. Data loading and computation have data dependencies, causing synchronization. The MTE loading can only be triggered after the Vector computation is completed, resulting in low parallelism. 2. Within the operator, there are no multiple data loads or no Tiling partitioning after a single execution, making it impossible to enable multi-buffer in this scenario. 3. Multi-buffer requires additional UB space usage. If there is insufficient UB space during computation, multi-buffer cannot be enabled."

msgid "二、代码示例"
msgstr "2. Code Example"

msgid "示例1：减少同步，提升并行度"
msgstr "Example 1: Reduce synchronization to increase parallelism"

msgid "在算子调优过程中，增加指令并行度是算子调优的重要手段。在如下的tl.load语句中，当N > M时, load加载的数据只能填充部分data指向的tensor内存空间中，剩下未填充的部分，如果用户未指定other值，则GPU默认填充为0，为了减少用户迁移的适配工作，NPU保持行为和GPU一致。NPU会先用Vector核对data指向的全部内存空间设置为指定值(如果用户未指定other值，同样设置为0)，然后在使用MTE2指令搬运数据到data指向的部分内存空间，这样就会导致MTE2和Vector产生依赖，无法高效并行，影响性能："
msgstr "In the process of operator tuning, increasing instruction-level parallelism is an important means of optimization. In the following `tl.load` statement, when N > M, the data loaded by `load` can only fill part of the tensor memory space pointed to by `data`. For the remaining unfilled part, if the user does not specify an `other` value, the GPU defaults to filling it with 0. To reduce the adaptation effort for user migration, the NPU maintains behavior consistent with the GPU. The NPU first uses the Vector unit to set the entire memory space pointed to by `data` to the specified value (if the user does not specify an `other` value, it is also set to 0), and then uses the MTE2 instruction to move data to the partial memory space pointed to by `data`. This creates a dependency between MTE2 and Vector, preventing efficient parallelism and affecting performance."

msgid "为了提升性能，在load加载数据只能部分填充到指向的内存空间时，如果未填充的部分不影响后续的计算结果，可以在load语句中，添加care_padding=False来去掉默认值的填充，增加并行度，提升性能，上面算子的优化写法如下："
msgstr "To improve performance, when a load operation only partially fills the targeted memory space and the unfilled portion does not affect subsequent computation results, you can add `care_padding=False` to the load statement to skip default value padding, increase parallelism, and enhance performance. The optimized version of the above operator is as follows:"

msgid "示例2：在Triton算子内，使用for循环，增加Tiling，提升并行度"
msgstr "Example 2: Use a for loop within the Triton operator to add Tiling and improve parallelism."

msgid "在Triton算子编程中，mask运算经常运用在load/store/where等语法中，在性能优化过程中，需要特别注意这类运算导致的性能下降。当Triton算子内逻辑是单次顺序执行，开始->数据搬入->计算->数据搬出->结束，指令无法并行，执行效率低;可以通过在算子使用for循环增加tiling，将单次处理量减少，多次处理，能够让\"数据搬入/计算/数据搬出\"并行起来，减少串行的等待时间，提升整体性能；同时使用for循环增加Tiling，也能降低单次处理消耗的UB空间。   需要注意：增加数据Tiling也同时需要考虑改变数据切块后的数学是否等价。"
msgstr "In Triton operator programming, mask operations are frequently used in syntax such as load/store/where. During performance optimization, special attention must be paid to the performance degradation caused by such operations. When the logic within a Triton operator is a single sequential execution—start → data load → computation → data store → end—instructions cannot be parallelized, resulting in low execution efficiency. By using a for loop to add tiling in the operator, the single processing volume can be reduced, and multiple processing steps allow \"data load/computation/data store\" to be parallelized, reducing serial waiting time and improving overall performance. At the same time, using a for loop to add tiling can also reduce the UB space consumed per single processing. Note: When adding data tiling, it is also necessary to consider whether the mathematics after changing the data partitioning remains equivalent."

msgid "数据类型优化"
msgstr "Data Type Optimization"

msgid "一、数据类型优化核心原则"
msgstr "I. Core Principles of Data Type Optimization"

msgid "A2/A3 向量运算单元的部分运算操作不支持某些数据类型，这种场景下，对应的向量运算会退化为标量运算，影响性能。在确定不影响整体算子精度的情况下，建议使用支持的数据类型，提升性能。 主要涉及以下操作"
msgstr "The A2/A3 vector arithmetic unit does not support certain data types for some operations. In such cases, the corresponding vector operations degrade to scalar operations, impacting performance. If it does not affect the overall operator precision, it is recommended to use supported data types to improve performance. This mainly involves the following operations."

msgid "**OP名称**"
msgstr "**OP Name**"

msgid "**不支持的数据类型**"
msgstr "**Unsupported Data Types**"

msgid "Vector ADD"
msgstr "Vector ADD"

msgid "int64"
msgstr "int64"

msgid "Vector CMP"
msgstr "Vector CMP"

msgid "int64/int32"
msgstr "int64/int32"

msgid "Vector Add Triton算子示例代码"
msgstr "Vector Add Triton Operator Example Code"

msgid "如下Triton算子，当x, y input tensor使用的数据类型是int64时，会导致x1+y1运算展开为Scalar运算，降低性能，在不影响精度的情况下，建议使用int32数据类型。"
msgstr "For the following Triton operator, when the data type used by the x and y input tensors is int64, the x1+y1 operation will be expanded into scalar operations, reducing performance. Without affecting precision, it is recommended to use the int32 data type."

msgid "Vector Cmp Triton算子示例代码"
msgstr "Vector Cmp Triton operator example code"

msgid "如下Triton算子，做mask运算时，使用到了Cmp操作，Cmp不支持int64/int32数据类型，会导致cols < N运算展开为Scalar运算，降低性能，在不影响精度的情况下，建议使用fp32数据类型。   在Triton算子编程中，mask运算经常运用在load/store/where等语法中，在性能优化过程中，需要特别注意这类运算导致的性能下降。"
msgstr "For the following Triton operator, when performing mask operations, the Cmp operation is used. Cmp does not support int64/int32 data types, which may cause the cols < N operation to be expanded into a Scalar operation, reducing performance. Without affecting precision, it is recommended to use the fp32 data type. In Triton operator programming, mask operations are often used in syntax such as load/store/where. During performance optimization, special attention should be paid to the performance degradation caused by such operations."
